       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose. You could titrate up to 10 mg.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if it's intentional. I'd add a note with the rationale, and I need your explicit confirmation first.\n\nIf 10 mg isn't controlling the blood pressure, you could add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic. That is usually preferred over going above 10 mg.\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed, and I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
